200.description:
Always returned, even when individual sub-requests fail. The body is an object keyed by each sub-request's `alias`.

Example body for the request example above (an invoice fetched by `show` and its requisitions fetched by `list`):

```json
{
  "invoice": {
    "id": 172185,
    "no": "INV-000123",
    "custom_data": null
  },
  "requisition": {
    "current_page": 1,
    "data": [ { "id": 991, "order_id": 172185, "order_type": 3 } ],
    "per_page": 20,
    "total": 1,
    "last_page": 1
  }
}
```

A sub-request that fails appears as an error object under its alias, e.g. `{ "requisition": { "error": "You are not allowed to view this page" } }`.
